# Public keys authorized to HOST a session through this uptermd relay.
# Standard OpenSSH authorized_keys format: one public key per line
# (ssh-ed25519 AAAA... / ssh-rsa AAAA... / ecdsa-sha2-... AAAA...).
#
# This does NOT gate who may JOIN a session someone else is already
# hosting - that's controlled by the per-session token instead.
#
# Copy this file to `authorized_keys` (gitignored, same as .env) and add
# real keys. To authorize another machine later: append its public key
# (the contents of its ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub or similar) as a new line,
# then `docker compose restart uptermd` to pick up the change.
